Package: qesR
Type: Package
Title: Access Quebec Election Study Datasets
Version: 0.6.0
Maintainer: Thomas Gareau-Paquette <tg454@cornell.edu>
Authors@R:
    person(
      given = "Thomas",
      family = "Gareau-Paquette",
      role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
      email = "tg454@cornell.edu"
    )
Description: Load the Quebec Election Studies and related Quebec election
    surveys from their 'Dataverse' deposits ('Borealis' and the 'Harvard
    Dataverse') by study code. Each study is pinned to one dataset version
    and one original 'SPSS' or 'Stata' data file, checked by its 'MD5'
    checksum before use. An offline catalog lists the studies, their
    documents and their citations, and shipped metadata give codebooks,
    question wording and search in English and French without network
    access. An experimental engine harmonizes selected variables across
    studies from a reviewed specification only, with each study's waves,
    weights and comparability grades, and returns survey designs for the
    'survey' and 'srvyr' packages. Data come from the Quebec Election
    Studies of 2007 (Bélanger et al. 2023) <doi:10.5683/SP2/6XGOKA>, 2008 (Bélanger and Nadeau 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/8KEYU3>, 2012 (Bélanger et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/WXUPXT>, 2014 (Bélanger and Nadeau 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/64F7WR>, 2018 (Bélanger et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/NWTGWS> and 2022 (Mahéo et al. 2023)
    <doi:10.7910/DVN/PAQBDR>; the panel surveys on the 2007 and 2012
    Quebec elections (Durand and Goyder 2023) <doi:10.5683/SP3/NDS6VT>
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/RKHPVL> and on the 2018 election (Durand and Blais
    2023) <doi:10.5683/SP3/XDDMMR>; the 'CROP' polls of 2007-2010 (Durand 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP3/IRZ1PF>; and the 1998 election polls (Durand 2023)
    <doi:10.5683/SP2/QFUAWG>. The studies are catalogued by the Centre for
    the Study of Democratic Citizenship
    <https://csdc-cecd.ca/portail-quebecois-sur-lopinion-publique/>.
